I wouldn't immediately deploy a giant predictive model.

Start with explainable models:

Logistic Regression
Random Forest
XGBoost
DBSCAN
Isolation Forest

Depending on the actual problem.
eg:
Crime records
      ↓
Feature engineering
      ↓
XGBoost
      ↓
Risk score
      ↓
Explainability
      ↓
Human officer

Use SHAP where appropriate to explain model contributions.

12. Very important: don't let "prediction" become autonomous policing

This is one of the places I'd draw a hard engineering boundary.

The system should not say:

"This person will commit a crime."

Instead:

"Historical records show a higher concentration of this crime type in these locations/time windows."

And even then:
Prediction
    ↓
Confidence
    ↓
Evidence
    ↓
Human review

No autonomous enforcement decisions
